Keep managed outgoing image descriptors out of model replay.

Base: OpenClaw v2026.8.1 (ea806575e6450e4d1efdfc72c19f04be982a1b9b).
The display-only URL/artifact blocks intentionally have no base64 data.
Treating them as model images creates a session:history diagnostic which models
can copy into user-facing answers. Drop only recognized assistant descriptors
from the in-memory replay copy; preserve stored attachments and actual inputs.
Also remove old standalone echoes, preserving quotes and fenced code examples.
Remove when upstream normalizes managed assistant image descriptors before
sanitizeSessionMessagesImages at all model replay boundaries.

